<title>FINLAND: FINNISH BANKS' MARKKA LENDING ROSE IN JUNE -C.BANK.</title>
<headline>FINNISH BANKS' MARKKA LENDING ROSE IN JUNE -C.BANK.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1997-08-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Banks' new lending to the public</p>
<p>rose in June to 10.72 billion markka from 8.87 billion in May,</p>
<p>the Bank of Finland said in its monthly financial markets review</p>
<p>received on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The stock of credits at the end of June was 265.46 billion,</p>
<p>down from 265.47 a month earlier, it said.</p>
<p>It gave the following figures:</p>
<p>Finnish banks' markka credits (FIM bln unless stated):</p>
<p>						June	  May</p>
<p> Total new credits			10.72	 8.87</p>
<p>  average interest rate		 4.93%	 4.96%</p>
<p> Stock of credits to public	   265.46	265.47</p>
<p>  average interest rate		 5.59%	 5.62%</p>
<p> New credits to households	    4.14	  4.13</p>
<p>  average interest rate		 5.87%	 5.89%</p>
<p> Stock of credits to households     152.67	152.52</p>
<p>  average interest rate		 6.22%	 6.25%</p>
<p>-- Helsinki newsroom +358-9-680 50 245, news@reuters.fi</p>
